<title>USA: US Treasury's 3, 6-mo bills seen at 5.19/5.38 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury's 3, 6-mo bills seen at 5.19/5.38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's sale of $24.0 billion in three- and six-month bills is expected to produce average rates of about 5.19 and 5.38 percent, respectively, dealers said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In when-issued trading before the 1300 EDT/1700 GMT bidding deadline, three-month bills were trading at 5.18 percent, while six-month bills were trading at 5.38 percent.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
